body:
**Link to problem area**: https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec/blob/main/content/client-server-api/modules/threading.md?plain=1#L15

**Issue**
What is wrong?

The spec says you can't make a thread based on a reply:

> It is not possible to create a thread from an event which itself
> is the child of an event relationship (i.e., one with an `m.relates_to`
> property). It is therefore also not possible to nest threads.

But Element Web allows threads to be created with replies as thread root:

![image](https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec/assets/76812/d68d6b95-1f98-42dd-a3df-5777a99c2d1c)

The reply and thread events shown above look like:

```
Event ID: $8UHA1RWgo_0r5V1gohzjPfupGCJI-SZQc8OqjATmelU
{
  "type": "m.room.message",
  "content": {
    "msgtype": "m.text",
    "body": "> <@x:y.co> Message\n\nReply to message",
...
    "m.relates_to": {
      "m.in_reply_to": {
        "event_id": "$E7IFEzhoNhXMr14TkrTbXtWCQoMEeVgdCyJJWG9a4Rs"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

```
Event ID: $q0UI_f7kEAW3E6X19wCFzplwksWTaYG15frgdjpgeko
Thread Root ID: $8UHA1RWgo_0r5V1gohzjPfupGCJI-SZQc8OqjATmelU
{
  "type": "m.room.message",
  "content": {
    "msgtype": "m.text",
    "body": "Thread from reply",
    "m.mentions": {},
    "m.relates_to": {
      "rel_type": "m.thread",
      "event_id": "$8UHA1RWgo_0r5V1gohzjPfupGCJI-SZQc8OqjATmelU",
      "is_falling_back": true,
      "m.in_reply_to": {
        "event_id": "$8UHA1RWgo_0r5V1gohzjPfupGCJI-SZQc8OqjATmelU"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

So the thread root is the reply event.

Here is the exchange with Synapse:

```
GET https://matrix-client.matrix.org/_matrix/client/v1/rooms/!OQYixnWsCXQExbbeWl%3Abeta.matrix.org/relations/%248UHA1RWgo_0r5V1gohzjPfupGCJI-SZQc8OqjATmelU/m.thread?dir=b&limit=2

200

{
  "chunk": [
    {
      "content": {
        "ciphertext": "...",
        "m.relates_to": {
          "event_id": "$8UHA1RWgo_0r5V1gohzjPfupGCJI-SZQc8OqjATmelU",
          "is_falling_back": true,
          "m.in_reply_to": {
            "event_id": "$q0UI_f7kEAW3E6X19wCFzplwksWTaYG15frgdjpgeko"
          },
          "rel_type": "m.thread"
        },
        ...
      },
      "event_id": "$TWdaar0SQQTHbveDWg3ZyAIn0nApyMHUjnLAAcimSTQ",
      ...
    },
    {
      "content": {
        "ciphertext": "...",
        "m.relates_to": {
          "event_id": "$8UHA1RWgo_0r5V1gohzjPfupGCJI-SZQc8OqjATmelU",
          "is_falling_back": true,
          "m.in_reply_to": {
            "event_id": "$8UHA1RWgo_0r5V1gohzjPfupGCJI-SZQc8OqjATmelU"
          },
          "rel_type": "m.thread"
        },
        ...
      },
      ...
      "event_id": "$q0UI_f7kEAW3E6X19wCFzplwksWTaYG15frgdjpgeko",
    }
  ]
}
```

So Synapse is OK with it.

Element X displays it as a thread fallback, similar to other threads.

Nheko shows it as a thread (notice the little purple icon near the ticks):

![image](https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec/assets/76812/5b41e396-6c9e-4e98-83e3-6b326a7cfc20)

**Expected behaviour**

I think the spec should probably allow replies to be thread roots - I don't see any harm in it.

So the wording might become:

> It is not possible to nest threads: you are not allowed to create a thread
> from an event which itself is in a thread (see ... for the exact definition of
> when an event is in a thread).

This would allow any event except one that is in a thread to become a thread root, including reactions, edits etc. We might want to restrict it to just replies, but that seems a little messy.

This sentence, later in the same section would also need rewording:

> As shown, any event without a `rel_type` can become a thread root by simply referencing it
> using an `m.thread` relationship.

Maybe to:

> As shown, any event **not in a thread** can become a thread root by simply referencing it
> using an `m.thread` relationship.
